      },
      "worked": "Reflecting first in the $x$-axis and then in the $y$-axis gives\n$$\\begin{align*}g(x)&=-f(-x)\\\\g(x)&=-\\frac{-x-4}{-x-1}\\\\g(x)&=-\\frac{x+4}{x+1}\\end{align*}$$\nAt an intersection, $f(x)=g(x)$, with $x\\ne\\pm1$:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{x-4}{x-1}&=-\\frac{x+4}{x+1}\\\\(x-4)(x+1)&=-(x+4)(x-1)\\\\x^2-3x-4&=-x^2-3x+4\\\\2x^2&=8\\\\x&=\\pm2\\end{align*}$$\nSubstituting into $f$, $f(-2)=2$ and $f(2)=-2$. The intersection points are $(-2,2)$ and $(2,-2)$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
